<!doctype linuxdoc system>

<article>

<!-- Title information -->

<title>Iindex
<author>Archibald Warnock <htmlurl url="mailto:awww@home.com"
  name="awww@home.com">, A/WWW Enterprises
<date>v1.41, 15 May 1998

<!-- Begin the document -->
<p>
<verb>
Iindex -d dbname [-V][-t doctype][-m NN][-s "sep"][-r][-o opt][files|-f filelist|-f -]
</verb>

<p>

<descrip>
<tag/Examples:/Iindex -d POETRY *.doc *.txt
<tag/ /Iindex -d WEBPAGES -t SGMLTAG *.html
</descrip>

<descrip>
<tag/[-d (X)]/ Use (X) as the root name for database files.
<tag/[-t (X)]/ Index as files of document type (X).
<p>
Document Types Supported:
<itemize>
<item>BIBTEX   
<item>COLONDOC        
<item>DIF     
<item>EMACSINFO       
<item>FGDC
<item>FGDCSITE
<item>FILENAME        
<item>FILMLINE        
<item>FIRSTLINE       
<item>FTP     
<item>GOPHER 
<item>HTML 
<item>IAFADOC         
<item>IKNOWDOC   
<item>IRLIST  
<item>LISTDIGEST 
<item>MAILDIGEST   
<item>MAILFOLDER      
<item>MEDLINE         
<item>MEMODOC         
<item>ONELINE         
<item>PARA    
<item>REFERBIB        
<item>SGMLNORM        
<item>SGMLTAG         
<item>SIMPLE  
<item>USMARC  
</itemize>
<tag/[-V]/ Print the version number.
<tag/[-m (X)]/ Load (X) megabytes of data at a time for indexing (default=1).
<tag/[-s (X)]/ Treat (X) as a separator for multiple documents within a single file.
<tag/[-f (X)]/ Read list of file names to be indexed from file (X).
<tag/[-r]/ Recursively descend subdirectories.
<tag/[-o (X)]/ Document type specific option.
<tag/(X) (Y) (...)/ Index files (X), (Y), etc.
</descrip>
<p>
</article>